stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> DRAFT: raised on an open exception, or an allowed reason code
    DRAFT --> PENDING: submitted, the day is in an open period
    DRAFT --> PENDING_RETRO: submitted, the day is inside a locked period
    PENDING --> PENDING: a level approves, further levels remain
    PENDING --> APPLIED: final approval writes a dated correction event
    PENDING --> REJECTED: rejected with a reason, the exception stays open
    PENDING --> WITHDRAWN: withdrawn by the creator
    PENDING --> ESCALATED: reg_approval_timeout_h elapses
    ESCALATED --> APPLIED: decided at the escalation level
    ESCALATED --> REJECTED: decided at the escalation level
    PENDING_RETRO --> APPLIED_RETRO: final approval plus retro authority
    PENDING_RETRO --> REJECTED: rejected with a reason
    APPLIED --> SUPERSEDED: a later regularization for the same day applies
    APPLIED --> REVERSED: compensating correction, period still open
    APPLIED_RETRO --> REVERSED: a further retro diff, never a mutation
    PENDING --> UNRESOLVABLE_SOURCE_ERASED: the day's punches passed retention
    REJECTED --> [*]
    WITHDRAWN --> [*]
    SUPERSEDED --> [*]
    REVERSED --> [*]
    UNRESOLVABLE_SOURCE_ERASED --> [*]
    note right of APPLIED_RETRO
        Emits a retro diff, an arrears input to
        section 08, and a new register version.
        The locked projection is never rewritten.
    end note
    note right of PENDING
        An open item blocks the period lock.
        A forced lock records the item and
        the forcing actor.
    end note
